  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-team-superflow",
      "text": "**A fixed five-member development team · driven by the spec-superflow state machine · live progress in the Web GUI**\n\nSpin up the same fixed dev team every time you use AgentTeams in DeepSeek Harness: a captain (the current session) plus five members, with the team's work flowing through spec-superflow's eight workflow states, visualized as a stepper in the activity panel."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-team-superflow",
      "text": "Refactored from [NanmiCoder/dsh-agent-teams](https://github.com/NanmiCoder/dsh-agent-teams), integrating the state-machine model of [MageByte-Zero/spec-superflow](https://github.com/MageByte-Zero/spec-superflow)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/demo1.png\" alt=\"Demo 1\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/demo2.png\" alt=\"Demo 2\" style=\"max-width: 420px; width: 100%;\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/demo3.png\" alt=\"Demo 3\" style=\"max-width: 420px; width: 100%;\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Fixed roster",
      "text": "Every `agent_teams_create` registers the same five members (subagents spawn lazily on their first phase-eligible dispatch):\n\n| member | role | active phases |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| spec-writer | spec writer | exploring · specifying · bridging |\n| architect | designer / architect | specifying · bridging |\n| engineer | engineer | executing · debugging |\n| reviewer | reviewer | executing · debugging |\n| docs | release / docs | executing · closing |"
    },
    {
      "section": "State machine",
      "text": "The team record persists the spec-superflow eight-state workflow:\n\n```text\nexploring → specifying → bridging → approved-for-build → executing ⇄ debugging → closing\n                                    │\n                                    └─ build gate: HUMAN approval before executing\n(any non-terminal state) ─────────→ abandoned (terminal)"
    },
    {
      "section": "State machine",
      "text": "- **Auto-advance**: when every task of the current phase completes, the team moves to the next phase (`phaseAutoAdvance`, default on).\n- **Build gate (human review)**: implementation freezes at `approved-for-build` until a human reviews the execution-contract artifacts and clicks 「批准构建」 in the Web panel. The model cannot confirm the gate itself.\n- **Rewind**: the captain may move back to `specifying` (scope change) or `bridging` (contract drift); a bug moves `executing → debugging` and returns automatically after fixes.\n- **Phase-tagged tasks**: `agent_teams_create_task` tags each task with a phase (default: current); the scheduler only dispatches tasks matching the current phase and the member's role scope."
    },
    {
      "section": "State machine",
      "text": "The activity panel adds a **state-machine stepper** (eight phase pills, overall percent, per-phase task counts, build-gate badge) refreshed from the durable host state."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "> Requires [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Method A: install straight from a git repo (recommended; GitHub or Gitee)",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://gitee.com/quella01/dsh-team-superflow.git"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/fengbin01/dsh-team-superflow.git",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Method B: clone and link locally (edit code, changes apply as you rebuild)",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://gitee.com/quella01/dsh-team-superflow.git ~/dsh-team-superflow\ndsh plugin --profile web add link:~/dsh-team-superflow\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Method C: npm package (after publishing; not published yet)",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-team-superflow\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Natural language:\n\n> Use AgentTeams to add a dark mode to this repo, following spec → contract → implement → review.\n\nOr the slash command:\n\n```\n/agent-teams refactor the auth boundary and produce the full execution contract and tests\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Capability |\n| --- | --- |\n| `agent_teams_create` | Create a team: registers the fixed five-member roster, starts in exploring, and materializes the spec-superflow artifact directory |\n| `agent_teams_add_member` | Add an extra member beyond the fixed roster (optionally scoped to workflow phases) |\n| `agent_teams_remove_member` | Safely remove a member: revoke its open tasks, interrupt its turn, mark it removed |\n| `agent_teams_create_task` | Create a phase-tagged task with dependencies (defaults to the current phase; blocked until deps complete) |\n| `agent_teams_reassign_task` | Atomically retry/reassign/take over a task, revoking the old attempt so late results cannot overwrite |\n| `agent_teams_claim_task` | Claim one ready task and receive the `attempt_id` capability |\n| `agent_teams_update_task` | Advance task status/output; when every current-phase task completes, the team auto-advances |\n| `agent_teams_send_message` | Direct captain/member messaging through durable mailboxes |\n| `agent_teams_status` | Read the current phase, per-phase progress, member activity, tasks, artifacts, and build-gate state |\n| `agent_teams_advance_phase` | Advance/rewind the state machine (d"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml\n- id: agent-teams\n  config:\n    stateDir: .agent-teams\n    memberProvider: spawn"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
